 "texts": [
  "Saffer, son tus huellas the path and you have everything; wanderer, there is no path it is made on the move.",
  "Way-wearer, they are the tracks that make the path, way-wearer, there is no road, you make the road as you walk.",
  "Walker, your footprints are the path, and nothing more, walker, there is no path, you make the path as you walk.",
  "Traveler, your footprints are the path and nothing more; traveler, there is no path, we make the path as we walk.",
  "Walker, it’s your footsteps the road, And nothing more, walker, there is no road, the road is made walking.",
  "Wanderer, your footprints are the way and nothing more; wanderer, no way, the way is made by walking.",
  "Walker, your footprints are the path and nothing more, walker, there is no path, as you walk, you make a path.",
  "Wayfarer, it is your feet that are the path, and nothing more; wayfarer, there is no path, the way is made by walking.",
  "Let the traveler be his own footprints on the road, traveler, there is no road, one makes it walking.",
  "Traveler, your footprints are the path, and nothing more; traveler, there is no path, walk it so you stay, the world is made up of Wanderers",
  "Pedestrian, it's your footprints the road and nothing more; Detour, there is no road, done road to go.",
  "Traveler, your footprints are the way and nothing else; traveler, there is no way, the way is made as you proceed.",
  "Traveller, your footprints are the road and that's all; traveller, there is no road, the road is made by walking.\nSpanish",
  "Walker, Your footprints are the track and nothing more, walker; no way exists, we make the track as we go.",
  "Walker, Your footprints are the way and nothing more; Walker, there is no road, you made the road by walking.",
  "Walker, your tracks are the road and nothing more; walker, there is no passage, it is made passage by the going.",
  "Traveler, your footprints are the way and only way; traveler, there is no road, you make the road by walking.",
  "Traveller, your steps are the road, and nothing else; traveller, there is no road, you make the road as you walk.",
  "Wayfarer, your own footprints are the road and nothing else. Wayfarer, there is no road, you make the road as you walk.",
  "Pilgrim, your footprints are the path and nothing more; pilgrim, there is no road, you make the road as you walk.",
  "The man who walks always finds the way.",
  "Traveler, your footprints are the path and nothing more; traveler, there’s no path, the road is made while walking.",
  "Traveler, yours are the footprints to follow, and nothing but your footprints, traveler, no trace of footprints you'll find, the path is made by walking.",
  "You must know, following the ancient rule from within yourself, how hundreds of ways of action all reach to fulfilment of the task.",
  "Traveler, your footprints are the path, and nothing more; traveler, there is no path, you make a path as you walk.",
  "A traveler, to your tracks are the road and no more; a traveler, there is no way, it is the path that makes the way is.",
  "Traveler, your footprints are the road and no more; traveler, there is no road, you make road as you go.",
  "Wayfarer, your footprints are the road, and nothing else; wayfarer, there is no path, one makes the path as he walks.",
  "Traveller, yours are the footprints that build the path and nothing else; traveller, there is no path, one builds the path whilst moving forward.",
  "Traveler, your footprints are the path and nothing more; traveler, there is no path, you create it as you walk.",
  "In a walker, Your tracks are the path and nothing more; in a walker there is no path, Path is made by walking.",
  "From the Spanish Camino de Santiago (David Jarrett): Walker, there is your path, and no more; walker, there's no more path, one makes the path by walking. This is taken by many as an indication to only set out on authentic travel… path-making.",
  "Traveler, your own footprints are the path and nothing more; traveler, there's no path and one makes the path as one goes.",
  "Pilgrim, it is your footprints that make the path. More not by not lowered to the ground; pilgrim, there is no path, by walking you make the world.",
  "The fugitive, your footprints are the road and nothing else; fugitive, there is no road, the road is built with every step taken.",
  "Traveler, your footprints are the path and nothing more; Traveler, there is no path, one makes it by walking.",
  "Traveler, are your footprints the road and nothing more; traveler, there is no road, but you make road as you follow it.",
  "Bartholomew, are your footprints the path and nothing else; traveler, there is no path, the path is made by walking.",
  "Wayfarer, your footprints are the path and nothing else; Wayfarer, there is no path, one makes a path while walking.",
  "Traveller, your footprints are the path, nothing more; traveller, there is no road, a path is a path as it is made.",
  "Wayfarer, your footprints are your route and nothing more; Wayfarer, there’s no route, route is made as going.\nSpanish",
  "Walker, your footprints are the way and that’s all: walker, there is no road, you pave the road while you walk.",
  "Walker, your trails are the path and nothing more; walker, there is no path, you make path with walking.",
  "Traveler, your footprints are the way and nothing else; Traveler, there is no way, you make the road while you travel.",
  "Walker, your footprints are the road and no more; walker, there is no road, the road is made as you walk.",
  "Looking closely at the map shows only what there is and where it is. But the map does not and cannot show what is yet to come.",
  "Wandering, it is your footprints the way; traveling, there is no way; way is made by walking.",
  "Travelling person, your footprints are the road, and naught else; travelling, no road is there, there is but travelling by trilocks",
  "Walkman, your footprints are the way and nothing more; Walkman, there is no way out, the way is made as you walk.",
  "Wayfarer, your footprints are the path and nothing more, wanderer, there is no path, you make the path as you step down",
  "Wanderer, your footprints are the road and nothing else; wanderer, there is no road, the road is made by walking.",
  "Seeker, your footprints are the road and nothing else; seeker, there is no road, there is no road, there is no road, there is no road, there is no road",
  "Wayfarer, your footprints are the way, and nothing else; wayfarer, there is no way, for us to walk the way let us build it as we walk.",
  "The walker, it is your footprints the way and nothing more; walker, there is no road, the road is done walking.",
  "Walkers, your tracks are the road and nothing else; walkers, there is no road, the road is made by walking.",
  "Wanderer, your footprints are the road and nothing else; wanderer, there is no road, paths are built as we travel.",
  "Traveler, your footprints are the way and nothing more; traveler, there is no road, you make the road as you go.",
  "Wanderer, your road was what you've walked over, and nothing more. Wanderer, there's no path. You have to create a path as you go on.",
  "Traveler, your footprints are the path and nothing more; traveler, there is not path, you create the path as you walk.",
  "Wanderer, your footprints are the road and that's all;\nStrayer, no road exists, one can only create one while walking.",
  "Walker, your steps are the way, and nothing more, walker, there is no path, the path is made by walking.",
  "Traveler, your footsteps are the road and nothing more; traveler, there is no road, a path is made by walking.",
  "Wayfarer, your footprints the path and no more:Wayfarer, there is no path, get onto the path and walk.",
  "Traveller, you are your own path and nothing more; Traveler, there is no path, one creates by walking."
 ],
